    "findings": [
      "All twelve boards were directly read. 22r2 has projected gray bases, orange object and red direction arrow, four page surfaces with one orange update, and a colored G-buffer stack. These are resource questions rather than actual measured performance.",
      "22r3 presents six separated condition plates: engine/API, camera, render path, feature settings, internal/output resolution and exposure/cache. Teal markers rise without implying a measured benchmark.",
      "22r4 shows distinct projected mip 0/1/2 surfaces with 4x4, 2x2 and 1x1 cells. Layer/depth/cubemap selection is explicitly separated from mip level. Surface elevation preserves visible top/front/side faces and labels.",
      "Boundary frames 929/930, 1767/1768 and 2688/2689 show the old last and new first scenes at the intended integer frame; adjacent samples and final frame 3836 retain readable black/white/yellow styling.",
      "23-pre-capture-dataflow shows the same Frame622/EID14 COLOR input (.96125,.01312,.02562,1), return input.color and SV_Target as three projected blocks. Orange and teal arrows appear in narration stages; input/output values match at the completed stage. The caveat correctly limits this to the observed simple color return, not proof of an entire lighting pass.",
      "These are clean source samples without burned narration captions. Continuous moving review, final composited pixels, final mixed ASR and delivery remain pending."
    ],
